# What Docker must NOT copy into the build.
#
# Everything the image needs is rebuilt inside it (npm ci, tsc, next build),
# so local build output would only add size — and worse, a host-built
# node_modules can contain Windows binaries that break on Linux.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets never go into an image. A layer is effectively public to anyone who
# can pull it, and deleting a file in a later layer does not remove it from
# the earlier one. Configuration arrives at RUN time, from the environment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
*.log
CLAUDE.md
LEARNINGS.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
